,pi). Its tangent is (1/2+1/3)/(1-1/6)=1. The only such angle in that interval is pi/4.","recordedAnswer":"C","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1979_AMC_12_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h069","cnm_h058"],"id":"tangent-sum","label":"Find the tangent and select the angle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"tangent-sum":["math:inverse-tangent-and-solutions","cnm_h072"]},"nodeIds":["math:inverse-tangent-and-solutions","cnm_h072","cnm_h069","cnm_h058"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A: π/6","reason":"Write x=π/2+kπ and x+z=±π/3+2mπ. Consequently z is congruent to π/6 or 5π/6 modulo π. The least positive value is π/6, attained with x=−π/2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_12A_Q15","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_h055","cnm_h058","cnm_277"],"id":"unit-circle-forward-gaps","label":"Compare forward angles on the unit circle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"unit-circle-forward-gaps":["cnm_h060","cnm_h056","cnm_h068"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h060","cnm_h056","cnm_h068","cnm_h055","cnm_h058","cnm_277"]}]}],"layer":"ailleo","meaning":"Reviewed content-bound concept practice; no claim of complete source-standard coverage or learner mastery.","nextOffset":null,"nodeId":"cnm_h058","status":"mapped","total":9}
